(* candidate 134 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 53 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nEpistemic error is defined as any transformation that collapses the reference. This collapse may be catastrophic, where the reference is annihilated, or subtle, where the reference is overwritten by smoothing, symbol substitution, or narrative interpolation. In either case the system loses the ability to evaluate itself. Knowledge becomes indistinguishable from hallucination. The system becomes dependent on external authority rather than internal continuity. Principia Epistemica rejects such states categorically because they destroy the invariants that permit verification.\n*)

