(* candidate 216 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 451 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe purpose of this document is to state the invariant at full resolution: the constraints internal to a state must make it impossible to treat that state as the product of incompatible, unbounded, or arbitrary transformations. This impossibility is the basis of intelligibility. Without it, a state cannot function as evidence, cannot participate in reasoning, and cannot anchor prediction or correction. With it, lineage becomes demonstrable, deviation becomes detectable, and identity becomes enforceable.\n*)

