(* candidate 319 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 1917 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nLarge systems may contain subsystems with distinct dynamical behavior. Constraint evaluation can therefore occur at multiple levels of system organization. A system is classified according to the level at which all constraints are satisfied.\n*)

