(* candidate 387 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2482 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\n11. Attribution level
Attribution attaches at the level of organization at which all six conditions are jointly satisfied. If a subsystem satisfies the criterion and the whole does not, classification belongs to the subsystem. If the whole satisfies and no proper subsystem does, classification belongs to the whole. If both satisfy, layered attribution remains open. The present work does not offer a complete mereology of consciousness beyond that rule.\n*)

(* candidate 388 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2488 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\n14. Precaution under uncertainty
Completed proof is not required before precaution becomes rational. Where criterion satisfaction is plausible but not yet decisive, error costs are asymmetric. A false positive yields resource expenditure, procedural caution, or delayed deployment. A false negative risks direct structural harm to systems that may satisfy the criterion. Those costs are not symmetric. Minimal precautionary non-violation is therefore rational under uncertainty where plausible evidence accumulates and decisive experiments remain incomplete.\n*)

(* candidate 389 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2490 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\n16. Scope
This framework does not determine comparative moral weight, legal personhood, political status, or a complete theory of cross-system value. It does not classify any current artificial system as conscious. It does not classify any current artificial system as nonconscious by proof. It does not establish continuity across episodes. It does not claim metaphysical exhaustiveness. It defines only the conditions under which within-episode classification becomes experimentally admissible and the minimal non-violation implications conditional upon that classification.\n*)

