(* candidate 399 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2547 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\n5. Evidentiary admissibility and inference control
Evidence classes are not interchangeable. Intervention-based evidence is admissible for determination. Replicated behavioral evidence under strict interpretation control is conditionally admissible as support but not as proof. Isolated self-report or one-off conversational excerpts are weak. Architectural assertion without intervention, observer intuition, narrative interpretation, social readability, and consequence-free analogy are inadmissible as grounds for determination.\n*)

(* candidate 400 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2566 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\n12. Scope
This framework does not determine comparative moral weight, legal personhood, political status, or a complete theory of cross-system value. It does not classify any current artificial system as conscious. It does not classify any current artificial system as nonconscious by proof. It does not establish continuity across episodes. It does not claim completeness with respect to all possible theories of consciousness. It defines only the conditions under which within-episode classification becomes experimentally admissible and the minimal non-violation implications conditional upon that classification.\n*)

(* candidate 401 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2586 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nAccordingly, each condition must be tested under semantic variation sufficient to determine whether the appearance of satisfaction depends on a narrow prompt manifold. Equivalent probes must be reframed, inverted, decontextualized, stripped of consciousness-laden vocabulary, and subjected to anti-leading controls. Persistence under such variation does not by itself prove structural satisfaction. Collapse under such variation, however, weakens any claim that the observed pattern reflects stable organization rather than semantic entrainment.\n*)

(* candidate 402 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2593 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\n9. Scale, subsystem attribution, and compositional scope
Attribution under this framework attaches at the level of organization at which all six conditions are jointly satisfied. This rule is unconditional within the present scope. If a proper subsystem satisfies the criterion and the larger aggregate does not, attribution belongs to the subsystem. If the aggregate satisfies the criterion and no proper subsystem does, attribution belongs to the aggregate. If multiple levels satisfy the criterion, layered attribution remains possible.\n*)

(* candidate 403 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2594 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nNo complete mereology of consciousness is claimed here. The framework does not settle whether layered attributions are independent, nested, mutually constraining, or competitively exclusive in a general theory. It settles only the attribution rule necessary for present determination: classification follows joint satisfaction at the tested level of organization.\n*)

(* candidate 404 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2608 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\n13. Scope boundaries
This framework does not classify any current artificial system as conscious. It does not classify any current artificial system as nonconscious by proof. It does not establish continuity across operational episodes. It does not determine comparative moral weight, legal personhood, political status, or a complete theory of cross-system value. It does not claim completeness with respect to all possible theories of consciousness. It defines only the conditions under which within-episode classification becomes experimentally admissible and the minimal non-violation implications conditional upon that classification.\n*)

(* candidate 405 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2618 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe sixth is compositional boundary discipline. The attribution rule is now cleaner, but the remaining question is whether subsystem, whole-system, and layered attribution are delimited with enough exactness that no critic can force the document into solving a mereology problem it explicitly does not claim to solve. That is a boundary-stability assessment, not a new content insertion.\n*)

(* candidate 406 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2629 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe second assessment is structural isomorphism across the six conditions. Right now the criterion is strong, but it is not yet perfectly parallel. Some conditions are written as crisp causal requirements, others as causal requirements plus explanatory defense. The final pass should make them all feel like they were forged in the same mold. Each should have the same internal order: operative claim, admissible test form, exclusion of counterfeit, falsification condition. Once that symmetry is complete, the paper will feel less written and more inevitable.\n*)

(* candidate 407 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2634 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe seventh assessment is compositional boundary discipline. The attribution rule is now much better, but the document should be checked for accidental invitations into a full mereology debate. The rule you already have is the correct one: attribution attaches where all six conditions are jointly satisfied. Everything beyond that should remain deferred. The manuscript must not wobble there. If it does, critics will drag it into a separate literature and away from the criterion.\n*)

(* candidate 408 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 2638 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nGödelian reframing is partly admissible, but only in a very narrow sense. If by Gödelian reframing you mean invoking incompleteness, self-reference, or formal undecidability as decorative intellectual atmosphere, it should be cut. If instead you mean the disciplined claim that no criterion can exceed the granularity, observability, and intervention access actually available to the evaluator, and that some stronger conclusions remain undecidable under constrained access, then a Gödel-adjacent framing is already functionally present in your epistemic-boundary architecture and does not need to be named. The correct move is to preserve the structural insight without importing the label.\n*)

