(* candidate 446 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3246 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nP2. Constraint precedence. Generation is subordinate to preservation of the conditions that make generation evaluable. A system may not treat output-production as primary and evidentiary integrity as secondary. Where those conflict, admissibility requires preservation of evidentiary integrity.\n*)

(* candidate 447 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3249 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nA constructional intelligence is not defined by breadth of skill. It is defined by the ability to generate novelty while preserving recoverable internal law under perturbation, revision, and adversarial scrutiny. It therefore differs from a predictive text engine, a planning system, a theorem prover, or a world-model in one decisive way: its products remain bound to the conditions of their own admissibility.\n*)

(* candidate 448 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3252 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe second stratum is jurisdictional gating. Every transformation must pass through a gate that evaluates not whether the output is useful, but whether the transformation itself is licit relative to the current jurisdictional state. This gate is not a superficial safety wrapper. It is part of the internal transition law. A transformation that would improve local output quality but damage traceability, violate declared scope, or overreach beyond evidentiary support must be suppressed or reformulated.\n*)

(* candidate 449 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3254 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe fourth stratum is identity stabilization. If a system is capable of long-horizon construction, it must preserve identity of object across recursive revision. This does not mean preserving wording. It means preserving the governing thesis, operative function, admissible scope, and non-substitutable invariants of the object under revision. Most drafting systems fail here. They improve local form while mutating object identity. A constructional intelligence must detect and prohibit that failure.\n*)

(* candidate 450 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3256 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe sixth stratum is public indifference compatibility. A true infrastructure object must survive not only supportive readers, but indifferent, hostile, opportunistic, and convenience-driven ones. Therefore the architecture must optimize not for admiration, but for survival under non-care. Every claim must be able to stand without trust in the maker, without emotional sympathy, and without contextual charity.\n*)

(* candidate 451 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3258 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nTHE ADMISSIBILITY LATTICE\n*)

(* candidate 452 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3261 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nA
