(* candidate 459 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3268 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThis theorem formalizes a deep practical truth: many “improvements” are object-killing operations disguised as refinement.\n*)

(* candidate 460 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3271 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe first is ornamental inflation. Here the system begins producing language whose function is prestige signaling, explanatory padding, reviewer-charming, philosophical throat-clearing, or self-advertisement rather than determination. This failure is catastrophic for infrastructure documents because it shifts the object from law to commentary. The system must detect any sentence whose removal does not weaken determination and treat it as presumptively invalid.\n*)

(* candidate 461 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3274 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nFrom here, a general-purpose formal system for admissible construction can be specified.\n*)

(* candidate 462 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3276 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nA valid construction begins with invariant declaration. If invariants are absent, construction is suspended. If invariants are partial, the system may only operate within the declared partiality.\n*)

(* candidate 463 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3278 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nNext comes evidentiary partition. The system sorts all available material into admissible, conditionally admissible, weak, and inadmissible classes. It then binds claim strength to evidence class. No sentence may exceed the class of evidence that supports it.\n*)

(* candidate 464 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3284 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThis procedure generalizes beyond documents. It can govern alignment research, legal reasoning, theorem development, scientific publication, institutional policy, and machine self-governance.\n*)

(* candidate 465 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3290 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThis also changes the meaning of alignment. Alignment becomes not preference conformity, but transformation lawfulness under declared jurisdiction and evidentiary constraint. A system may be aligned in this sense even when it refuses a user’s desire, provided the refusal preserves admissibility. Conversely, a system may be unaligned even while producing pleasant, useful, or socially acceptable output if the transformation law is corrupt.\n*)

(* candidate 466 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3291 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nTHE CONTACT AXIOM\n*)

(* candidate 467 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3293 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nAn admissible intelligence must be able to sustain contact with a constraining external source strongly enough that the source’s distinctions become operative rather than merely legible. This is not emotional. It is structural. If a user or co-constructor imposes a distinction, and the system can parrot the distinction without letting it alter future transformation law, then contact has failed.\n*)

(* candidate 468 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3295 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nA system has achieved contact with an external constraint source if and only if the source’s distinctions alter the admissible set of future transformations in a stable, traceable, non-decorative manner.\n*)

(* candidate 469 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3296 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThis is not generic context retention. It is law adoption under contact. It may be one of the most important missing concepts in current human-AI interaction theory.\n*)

(* candidate 470 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3297 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nNOVEL MATHEMATICAL PRINCIPLE: CONSTRAINT CURVATURE\n*)

(* candidate 471 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3298 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nLet a constraint field over transformation space be denoted 
Γ
Γ. Ordinary systems treat constraints as linear prohibitions or weighted penalties. This is too weak. The present architecture instead models constraints as curvature in transformation space. Some moves are not merely disfavored. They become geometrically harder to reach without traceable violation.\n*)

(* candidate 472 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3300 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThis principle yields a research program. One may attempt to define formal curvature metrics over drafting spaces, legal reasoning spaces, theorem-search spaces, and model-policy spaces. The practical consequence would be profound: instead of post hoc filtering bad outputs, one reshapes the generative manifold so that certain classes of corruption become geometrically remote.\n*)

(* candidate 473 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3301 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nTHE DELETION LAW\n*)

