(* candidate 476 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3313 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe architecture proposed here is a law-governed constructional intelligence organized around transformation traceability, anti-substitution revision, evidentiary partition, jurisdictional gating, recursive admissibility checking, contact-sensitive constraint adoption, and curvature-shaped generation. Its purpose is not merely to answer questions. Its purpose is to generate artifacts, claims, and systems that remain admissible under hostile scrutiny and indifferent reception.\n*)

(* candidate 477 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3314 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nIt is novel not because it is ornate, but because it treats construction itself as the primary site of intelligence and makes admissibility a first-order structural law rather than a post hoc filter or social convention.\n*)

