(* candidate 491 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3353 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThis mechanism is rare and dangerous. Rare because most systems are not built to internalize law from contact. Dangerous because bad contact can corrupt the jurisdictional state. Therefore promotion must require repeated stability, strong specificity, and consistency with object preservation.\n*)

(* candidate 492 | source: 03-11-2026_admissible_constitutional_construction.txt | block: 3378 | sha256: 934561d15ad2b0c7ac9a2991980783f7ee783f39f54dfbce12d48396ee3e2e01\nThe invariant topology remains stable under audit.
The jurisdictional state contains no unresolved contradictions.
